  "summary": "The paper proposes a single‑qubit quantum neural network classifier with MSFLA feature selection for credit card fraud detection on the Kaggle dataset (284,807 transactions, 491 fraud cases). The proposed model reports 97.06% accuracy, 96.94% F1‑score, 96.67% recall, and 97.23% precision, outperforming classical baselines such as CNN (95.78% accuracy) and LSTM (95.84% accuracy), though all experiments were run on classical hardware.",
